{
  "dom_id": "step-q75431",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If $\\frac{3}{7}x=6$, then $x=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}x & =6 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{3}{7}x & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\cancel{7}\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\cancel{7}}x & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\ 3x & =42\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $3$ to isolate $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3x & =42 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{42}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}x}{\\cancel{3}} & =\\frac{42}{3} \\\\ x & =14\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
